$O$ is the centre. $\angle AOB = 112^{\circ}$. Find $\angle ACB$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt) node[below right] {$O$};
\coordinate (A) at (-1.658,1.118);
\coordinate (B) at (1.658,1.118);
\coordinate (C) at (0,-2);
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below] at (C) {$C$};
\draw (O) -- (A);
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (C) -- (A);
\draw (C) -- (B);
\pic[draw, "$112^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.55cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = B--O--A};
\pic[draw, "$x$", angle radius=0.55cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = B--C--A};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

